# viola-plugin-abi: Design

Stable C-ABI contract surface for viola plugins. `#![no_std]`, zero allocations across the FFI boundary. All variable-length data crosses as `(ptr, len)` carriers into plugin-owned static memory whose lifetime equals the loaded library.

This crate is the foundation every viola plugin compiles against. The vtable shapes are append-only within an ABI major; adding a new function pointer registers a fresh `ProviderId` rather than mutating an existing vtable. The normative ABI spec lives at `docs/PLUGIN-ABI-V1-DESIGN.md`; this document summarises what the crate ships.

## Provider IDs

Three provider IDs that viola plugins implement against (the runner and grammar roles at v1, the lint role at v2). Each maps to one vtable shape and one viola role.

### `PROVIDER_RUNNER_EXECUTE_SCOPE`

`viola.runner.execute_scope.v1`. The runner-role provider id. Points at a `RunnerExecuteScopeVtable`. Plugins declaring this provider take a `RunScope` and produce a `NamPayload`.

### `PROVIDER_GRAMMAR_EXTRACT`

`viola.grammar.extract.v1`. The grammar-role provider id. Points at a `GrammarExtractVtable`. Plugins declaring this provider take a file plus source bytes and produce a `NamPayload` contribution.

### `PROVIDER_LINT_EVALUATE`

`viola.lint.evaluate.v2`. The lint-role provider id. Points at a `LintEvaluateVtable`. Plugins declaring this provider take a `NamPayload` plus lint config bytes and write findings into a host-owned `Diagnostic` buffer.

## Vtable shapes

Each vtable is a `#[repr(C)]` struct of concrete `extern "C"` function pointers. Append-only within an ABI major per `docs/PLUGIN-ABI-V1-DESIGN.md` §7.3.

### `RunnerExecuteScopeVtable`

Single function pointer `execute_scope(host_ctx, scope, out_nam)`. The runner role gets a `RunScope` wrapper because the spec names "configured run scope" as a domain concept that travels together.

### `GrammarExtractVtable`

Single function pointer `extract(host_ctx, file, source_bytes, source_len, out_contribution)`. Direct args (no wrapper struct) because the four inputs are independent values with no shared spec-named identity.

### `LintEvaluateVtable`

Single function pointer `evaluate(host_ctx, nam, lint_config_bytes, lint_config_len, out_entries, out_capacity, out_len) -> AbiStatus`. The host owns the output buffer: it passes a `*mut Diagnostic` slice (`out_entries`) with its `out_capacity` and an `out_len` pointer; the plugin writes through up to capacity. On overflow the plugin writes the first `out_capacity` entries, sets `*out_len` to the count it would have emitted, and returns `AbiStatus::Internal`; otherwise it sets `*out_len` to the written count and returns `AbiStatus::Ok`. Direct args (no wrapper struct). The 2026-05-23 three-specialist convergence settled the wrapper-vs-direct-args design Q in favour of direct args.

## Runner-role carriers

### `RunScope`

`#[repr(C)]` bundle the host hands the runner: workspace root, files slice, surface tag, ci flag. Stable wire shape across the FFI boundary; the host constructs it from its in-process Resources at the call site.

### `FileEntry`

`#[repr(C)]` per-file carrier inside the `RunScope.files` slice. Carries path, language, content hash, and size in bytes.

### `RunSurface`

`#[repr(u32)]` enum mirrored into NAM `run_context.surface`. Variants: `Cli`, `Hook`, `Ci`, `Lsp`, `Test`, `Other`.

## NAM carriers

The normalised analysis model the runner produces and the lints read.

### `NamPayload`

`#[repr(C)]` snapshot the host passes to lints. Carries pointers into NAM-formatted bytes that the runner produced.

### `NamVersion`

Version tag carried on the payload. Lets the host validate that runner and lint agree on the NAM schema version before invoking the lint.

## Diagnostic wire shape

The output a lint emits; the host sorts and renders. The host owns the output buffer and passes it to `evaluate` as `out_entries` (a `*mut Diagnostic` slice) plus `out_capacity`; the lint writes its records through and reports the count via `out_len`.

### `Diagnostic`

Single diagnostic record: severity, source location, message text, optional metadata.

### `DiagnosticSeverity`

Enum naming the severity levels.

### `SourceLocation` and `SourceRange`

Position carriers. `SourceLocation` is a single point (file, line, column). `SourceRange` is a pair of locations bounding an extent.

## Boundary helpers

### `BytesRef`

Two-word `(ptr, len)` carrier for byte slices crossing the FFI boundary. Identical pattern to hilavitkutin's name slice convention. References plugin-owned static memory stable for the loaded library's lifetime.

### `AbiStatus`

Historical alias for `hilavitkutin_extensions::ExtensionAbiStatus`. Preserves callsites that imported `AbiStatus` from this crate before the substrate rebase. New code should prefer the canonical `ExtensionAbiStatus`.

## Error envelope

### `PluginError`

`#[repr(u32)]` enum of viola-domain error categories. Variants: `RoleProviderMissing`, `ModelVersionMismatch`, `InvocationFailed`, `ConfigInvalid`. Distinct from `hilavitkutin_extensions::ExtensionError` which covers descriptor-level failures rather than viola-domain ones.

### `StructuredError`

`#[repr(C)]` envelope per `docs/PLUGIN-ABI-V1-DESIGN.md` §11. Carries code, message, schema id, details pointer, retryable flag.

## ABI versioning

The `ProviderId` is the version anchor. Adding a new optional hook or alternative dispatch shape registers as `viola.lint.evaluate.v2` rather than mutating v1. The `vtable_ptr` shape from `ProviderEntry` supports forward extension without breaking existing plugins.

## Re-exports

This crate re-exports the descriptor and lifecycle types from `hilavitkutin-extensions` so plugin authors compile against a single dependency surface. The re-exported set includes `ProviderEntry`, `ProviderExport`, `ProviderId`, `DESCRIPTOR_SYMBOL`, `ExtensionAbiStatus`, `ExtensionDescriptor`, `ExtensionMeta`, `ExtensionVersion`, `HOST_ABI_VERSION`, `InitHandler`, `ShutdownHandler`.
